menu "Pico FIDO - R558 fingerprint sensor"

config PICO_FIDO_R558_REQUIRE_FLASH_ENCRYPTION
    bool "Require ESP32 flash encryption before pairing or restoring the R558 sensor"
    default y
    help
        The R558 password and address are stored in flash. Without flash encryption, anyone who can
        read the flash can copy them and build a fake sensor (see docs/fingerprint/R558_PLAN.md, R1).
        With this option on, pairing and restoring are refused until flash encryption is active.
        Turn it off only for development boards that must not use flash encryption.

endmenu
